{
  "manufacturer": "Contemporary Controls",
  "manufacturer_slug": "contemporary-controls",
  "model": "Generac G-Panel generator control via BASgatewayLX",
  "short_model": "BASgatewayLX Generac G-Panel",
  "model_slug": "basgatewaylx-generac-g-panel",
  "aliases": [
    "G-Panel",
    "Generac G Panel",
    "Generac Modbus G-Panel"
  ],
  "equipment_type": "Generator set controller",
  "applies_to": "Generac generator sets with the G-Panel control (Modbus), read by a BASgatewayLX.",
  "summary": "Gateway profile for the Generac G-Panel: 197 objects (45 AI, 32 BI, 120 BO), 151 polled by default. Analog inputs give engine temperatures and pressures, fuel and coolant level, battery, bus and generator voltages, currents, kW, PF, frequency and rpm. The panel's status and alarm flags (common alarm, running, in auto, ready to accept load, each shutdown and warning) are mapped as Binary Outputs because they are Modbus coils.",
  "bacnet_transport": [
    "BACnet IP"
  ],
  "firmware": null,
  "default_device_instance": null,
  "access_inferred": true,
  "notes": [
    "Built from Contemporary Controls' BASgatewayLX Modbus device profile Generac_G_Panel__a_LX.csv; the profile maps the registers in the Generac G-Panel Modbus register list (https://www.ccontrols.com/support/dp/SupportFileGeneracGPanel.zip).",
    "Object instances are the ones this profile assigns when it is loaded into the gateway. A site that edited or rebuilt the profile may use different instances.",
    "Only 151 of the 197 rows are flagged for polling in the profile; the rest are served only after you tick them in the gateway. Their descriptions say \"not polled by default\".",
    "The CSV has no read/write column: Analog/Binary Inputs are read-only and Analog/Binary Outputs are commandable (priority array), which is how the gateway maps them (access inferred). Descriptions give the Modbus register each object reads.",
    "Some names appear more than once in the profile as published (USER CONFIGURABLE 08; USER CONFIGURABLE 09; BATTERY CHARGER FAIL); they are kept as printed and told apart by instance."
  ],
  "source": {
    "title": "BASgatewayLX Modbus device profile Generac_G_Panel__a",
    "doc_number": "Generac_G_Panel__a_LX.csv",
    "revision_date": null,
    "url": "https://www.ccontrols.com/support/dp/GeneracGPanel.zip"
  },
  "integration": {
    "summary": "Read RUNNING, GENERATOR IN AUTO, READY TO ACCEPT LOAD and COMMON ALARM (Binary Outputs here) plus generator kW and voltage.",
    "minimum_points": [
      {
        "ref": "BO 128",
        "name": "RUNNING",
        "why": "Generator running"
      },
      {
        "ref": "BO 122",
        "name": "GENERATOR IN AUTO",
        "why": "Generator in auto"
      },
      {
        "ref": "BO 129",
        "name": "READY TO ACCEPT LOAD",
        "why": "Ready to accept load"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AI 35",
        "name": "GEN TOTAL KW",
        "why": "Generator total kW"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AI 34",
        "name": "GEN AVERAGE VOLTAGE",
        "why": "Generator average voltage"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AI 39",
        "name": "GEN FREQUENCY",
        "why": "Generator frequency"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AI 18",
        "name": "BATTERY VOLTAGE",
        "why": "Battery voltage"
      },
      {
        "ref": "BO 76",
        "name": "COMMON ALARM",
        "why": "Common alarm"
      },
      {
        "ref": "BO 77",
        "name": "COMMON WARNING",
        "why": "Common warning"
      }
    ],
    "enable": null,
    "heartbeat": null,
    "remote_sensors": null,
    "setup": [
      "The BASgatewayLX presents each Modbus device as its own virtual BACnet device on BACnet IP; give it a unique device instance and Modbus address (serial) or IP address (Modbus TCP) when you add it with this profile.",
      "One BASgatewayLX handles up to 100 Modbus devices and 1000 polled points in total, so leave unneeded rows unpolled."
    ],
    "gotchas": [
      "Status and alarm flags are Binary Outputs (coils) in this profile; treat them as read-only and never write them.",
      "Unpolled rows do not appear as BACnet objects until enabled in the gateway's device profile page."
    ]
  },
